<QF id="PMS Performance Measurement_19" sectionNumber="" articleNumber="0" articleName="">
    <question>
        <text><![CDATA[Sharpe ratio is calculated as:]]></text>
        <answers>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[(Rp - Rf)/beta]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="yes"><text><![CDATA[(Rp - Rf)/sigma_p]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[(Rm - Rf)/sigma_p]]></text></answer>
            <answer correct="no"><text><![CDATA[Rp/sigma_p]]></text></answer>
        </answers>
        <explanation><text><![CDATA[**The Logic:** Sharpe = (Return - Risk-free) / Standard Deviation.
**The Trap:** Treynor uses beta in denominator.
**Cross-Exam Context:** Same in X-B.
**Distributor's Pro-Tip:** Use the same sigma period as returns to avoid annualisation mismatches.]]></text></explanation>
    </question>
</QF>
